; A 100 x 10 x 16.6 beam bent by a couple (about 50 MPa at its top and bottom
; faces), its top face at z 8.3: on cells of 1, 2 and 4 mm the cells holding
; that face are under half material, so its points are read from the cells
; under them, outside those cells' boxes, on every grid of the ladder. E is
; graded slightly along the beam (2.5% end to end), so no cell is of one
; material and min-safety-factor is a band from its bound. A layer
; z 8.2..8.3 under the top face (|x| < 40), of the same E, has yield 25
; (else 250): it carries the full bending stress at the face, so the factor
; there is about 25 / 50 = 0.5 (master reads it: the face read is its cells'
; peak). The bound takes the least yield over each cell's box, which never
; holds the layer.
; truth: safe fails about 0.46 (the layer, of the bulk's E, carries the full bending stress at the face; yield-graded-weak-face-deep-flat-e, E uniform: 0.465, converging)
; truth: unsafe holds about 0.46 (as safe)
(import "std")
(def part (box 100 10 16.6))
(def layer (max (- 8.2 z) (- z 8.5) (- (abs x) 40)))
(study s (shape part)
 (elastic (E (* 1MPa (+ 200000 (* 50 x)))) (nu 0.3) (yield (* 1MPa (select layer 25 250))))
 (fix root (+ x 49))
 (load top (force 2000N 0 0) (region (max (- 49 x) (- 4 z))))
 (load bottom (force -2000N 0 0) (region (max (- 49 x) (+ z 4))))
 (res 1))
(require safe (min-safety-factor s > 1))
(require unsafe (min-safety-factor s < 1))
